    "body": "It's currently not rending the tip correctly.\r\n\r\n- [x] This PR does not suggest changes based on personal taste (enabling new or changing value of existing option, install new plugin)\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2025-10-13T17:01:55Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the PR!\r\n\r\nAlthough I understand the frustration, I am afraid this is intended. The tip is related to the list item, so it has to be indented. While the GitHub doesn't support indented alert blockquotes, they are [properly converted](https://nvim-mini.org/MiniMax/#knowledge) into Quarto callout blocks on the site. As the main goal is for this to look the best on the nvim-mini.org site, I'll leave it for now. Maybe will keep this in mind to rework the whole bullet point altogether.",
